=== Minions ===
'''Purple Candy''' has a {{Green|0.015%}} chance to be obtained per item generated from [[Minions]] with the {{Item|Sleepy Hollow}} upgrade applied.

=== Trick or Treat Chests ===
Opening a [[Trick or Treat Chest]] has a {{Green|17.71%}} chance to grant 1-4 '''Purple Candy'''.

=== Party Chests ===
Opening a [[Party Chest]] has a {{Green|18.012%}} chance to grant 2-6 '''Purple Candy'''.

=== Great Spook Tree ===
A {{Item|Great Spook Tree}} can be placed on the player's {{Zone|Private Island}} to occasionally generate '''Purple Candy'''.

=== Garden Visitors ===
Accepting the {{NPCSprite|Fear Mongerer}}'s [[Garden Visitor]] request will grant a {{Item|Green Candy}} or '''Purple Candy'''.

== Usage ==
'''Purple Candy''' can be traded the [[Fear Mongerer]] while they are in the {{Zone|Village}} in exchange for spooky-themed items, as is the case with {{Item|Green Candy}}.

Obtaining '''Purple Candy''' awards the player {{Green|+5}} points in the [[Spooky Festival]], while {{Item|Green Candy}} only gives {{Green|1}} point. This is only the case for candies dropped directly from killing mobs or by collecting candies from Bats (excluding players' Bat Fireworks).

